From 3ea110f23060db48e827267848d25f02def6fb9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:15:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] static: don't complain about a nonexistent interface when
 downing it
Organization: Wires

Like the link executor.  The other end of a veth pair is gone along
with the first one, and its own turn to go down then fails on the
address flush, which keeps the rest of its teardown from running.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 executors/linux/static | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/executors/linux/static b/executors/linux/static
index 367fd3a..1f9f3de 100755
--- a/executors/linux/static
+++ b/executors/linux/static
@@ -50,6 +50,8 @@ up)
 	configure_gateways add
 	;;
 down)
+	# Don't complain about a nonexistent interface when downing it
+	[ -d "/sys/class/net/${IFACE}" ] || [ -n "${MOCK}" ] || exit 0
 	flush
 	;;
 *)	exit 0 ;;
